<main>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="page">
    <h1>Gus on Apple TV</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Browse your Jellyfin library with the Apple TV remote and native playback controls.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="page"><div class="content-grid"><div>
    <article class="content-block">
      <h2>Connect and navigate</h2>
      <p>Enter your server address, choose Connect and sign in with your Jellyfin account. Find a local server starts a local network search when selected. More sign-in options offers public profiles or Quick Connect when enabled by your server.</p>
      <p>Use the sidebar to change sections. Back/Menu closes the current task or returns to the previous screen. Movie details use a cinematic backdrop with synopsis and metadata on the left, and Play plus compact actions on the right. Series and seasons retain a left-aligned layout. More includes watched status and supported playlist/collection actions.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="content-block">
      <h2>Choose a theme</h2>
      <p>Settings provides System, Light and Dark appearance, plus a separate Theme section with Gus Default, Apple Default and Custom. Custom offers named accent presets or a six-digit hex color. Save applies your preview; Cancel keeps the previous color. These preferences stay on this Apple TV.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="content-block">
      <h2>Keep listening</h2>
      <p>Close Now Playing to return to browsing while prepared audio continues. Reopen it from the persistent Now Playing control. Stop ends playback; Queue opens track selection. Audio and video use native AVKit transport and output controls. Playback details have a contrast background over video.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="content-block">
      <p>Toolbar actions use familiar symbols with accessible names. Back follows system navigation; editor actions such as Save and Cancel retain descriptive text. Account uses the sidebar header on tvOS 27; profile and saved-account actions are in Settings on tvOS 26.</p>
      <h2>Server and device requirements</h2>
      <p>Apple TV streams media; downloads and an EPUB reader are unavailable. Live TV requires a configured tuner and guide. Audio and subtitle choices depend on the media. Discover has a separate Search Seerr page. Seerr setup, request review, confirmation and history identify the service; requests depend on the connected server and your permissions.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/eslutz/A-Playa-Named-Gus/wiki/Apple-TV">Read the full Apple TV guide</a> or <a href="/support/">get support</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div></div></section>
</main>
